{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":906,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Prov.19","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Proverbs","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Proverbs 19","reference":"Proverbs 19","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":2,"text":"Hasteth - That rashly and headily rushes into actions.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":3,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":4,"text":"Perverteth - Blasts his designs and enterprises.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":5,"text":"Fretteth - He ascribes his unhappiness not to his own sin, but to God and his providence.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":6,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":7,"text":"A friend - in profession.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":8,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":9,"text":"Brethren - His nearest relations.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":10,"text":"Hate - Despise and shun him.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":11,"text":"Pursueth - Earnestly imploring their pity.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":12,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":13,"text":"Delight - To live in pleasure and outward glory, doth not become him, nor suit with him; because prosperity corrupts even wise men, and makes fools mad; and because it gives him more opportunity to discover his folly, and to do mischief both to himself and others.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":14,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":15,"text":"Dropping - Are like rain continually dropping upon an house.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":16,"text":"15.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":17,"text":"Casteth - Makes a man careless, and like one asleep in his business.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":18,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":19,"text":"His ways - The commands of God.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":20,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":21,"text":"While - Before custom in sin, and thy indulgence have made him incorrigible.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":22,"text":"Let not - Forbear not to give him due and necessary correction.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":23,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":24,"text":"Great wrath - Of strong passions.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":25,"text":"Deliver - If thou forbear to punish him.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":26,"text":"Do it - Thou must deliver him again and again.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":27,"text":"22.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":28,"text":"The desire - The hearty desire of being kind is accepted by God, and should be owned by men as a real kindness.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":29,"text":"A poor man - Who is not able to give what he desires to do.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":30,"text":"A liar - Than a rich man who feeds the poor with fair promises, but doth not perform what he pretends.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":31,"text":"23.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":32,"text":"Satisfied - Shall be fully contented with God's favour and blessing.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":33,"text":"24.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":34,"text":"Bring it - To feed himself; he expects that the meat should drop into his mouth.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":35,"text":"25.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":36,"text":"Scorner - An obstinate and impudent transgressor.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":37,"text":"Simple - Who sin thro' ignorance, being possibly drawn to it by the scorner's evil counsel or example.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":38,"text":"Reprove - A verbal reproof will be more effectual for his reformation, than the severest punishments will be to a scorner.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":39,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":40,"text":"Wasteth - His father's estate.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":41,"text":"Chaseth - Causes her to avoid his presence, and to go from the house where he is.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":42,"text":"28.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":43,"text":"Scorneth - Hath no reverence to the place of justice, nor to the presence of God there.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":44,"text":"Devoureth - Utters it with greediness and delight.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":45,"text":"29.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":46,"text":"Prepared - Although they be deferred for a time, yet they are treasured up for them.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":19}}